}^{2}-5\\lambda +6 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda -2)(\\lambda -3)=0,\n$$\n\nand so the solutions of the auxiliary equation  are $\\lambda =2$ or $\\lambda =3.$\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{2x}$ and ${e}^{3x}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only $2{e}^{x}$ is not a solution."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357473 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d8134cb-757e-5d42-9e52-e1be730cd855" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{6x}+2{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354790} {:answer/id #uuid "3529b0ab-4f12-594c-a2f7-c68b64eaf2ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{6x}-8{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355139} {:answer/id #uuid "7d31d0c1-0468-5e56-877c-19e818ac36c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{6x-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355768} {:answer/id #uuid "d13b07b9-d726-574c-9d7e-e27a8da7875f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356495} {:answer/id #uuid "df457980-9f43-5760-a71d-325601bca0f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-{e}^{6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356618}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df457980-9f43-5760-a71d-325601bca0f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-{e}^{6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356618} :answer-field/id #uuid "019cf9ab-0c62-56d0-bba2-30385b4bf346" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356911}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "937412e4-d54f-5aaa-9272-a